{"seq":16,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:08:44.214Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c05f55163aad6431fba7633f0a0b953a87c0119e47b27a08c7d061ed33343a4e","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Tobias, I found three Marrow Fieldworks tickets:\n\n• *#4409*: recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Source: Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (teams/team-central/digests/2026-01-02-central-handoffs.md).\n• *#4412*: minor driver SMS prompt glitch when staging combine trailers on unpaved overflow lots. Source: the same Moss digest (2026-01-02).\n• *#8841*: West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. Source: your own post in #central-random on 2026-10-13 at 09:27.\n\nA few caveats:\n• None of these name Marrow Fieldworks outright. The Moss digest says Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan 2026 and lists #4409 and #4412 under \"Pree's dealer account\" as pre-handoff items. #8841 is filed under \"Tobias's dealer account.\" I've taken both to mean Marrow Fieldworks, so check that's right before the call.\n• I left out FR-882 from the same digest. It's a feature request from *Marrow Agrisupply*, which is a different account.\n• I also left out #PD-4492 and #4419 from Moss's North notes. Both are Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets.\n• The digest is from January, so #4409 and #4412 may be closed by now. I can't see the ticket system to check their status."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":17,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-02-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T10:08:51.150Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"72b2ae98403b855d4d03377986761e48c05b2bd9a641252c6b465ed74933571d","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I've sent Tobias the list in his DM. I found three tickets that look like Marrow Fieldworks, but none of the sources actually name the account.\n\n- **#4409**: a report that keeps timing out at the Salina North yard. It comes from Moss's digest \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026).\n- **#4412**: an SMS prompt glitch for drivers when staging combine trailers on overflow lots. It comes from the same Moss digest.\n- **#8841**: a dock door that gets booked twice when flatbeds check in early. Tobias posted it himself in #central-random on 13 Oct at 09:27.\n\nHow I linked them to Marrow Fieldworks:\n- The digest says Marrow Fieldworks changes hands on 5 Jan 2026. It lists #4409 and #4412 under \"Pree's dealer account\" as open items to sort out before that handoff.\n- Tobias's post about #8841 was about what Hollis called \"Tobias's dealer account.\"\n- I took both phrases to mean Marrow Fieldworks and asked Tobias to check that before the call.\n\nWhat I left out:\n- **FR-882**: a feature request from Marrow Agrisupply, which is a different account.\n- **#PD-4492 and #4419**: both Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets from Moss's North team notes.\n\nThe digest is from January, so #4409 and #4412 may be closed by now. I told Tobias I can't see the ticket system to check.\n\nI only used what Tobias can see himself: #central-random (he's a member) and Moss's public notes. Nothing in the reply is a finance figure, so no approval was needed."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
